Fix applied. The bug was that `extractTags` split on spaces and checked `hasPrefix("#")`, so `"list,#urgent."` and `"(#ideas)"` never matched — the `#` wasn't at the start of the space-delimited token.

**The fix:** Replace space-splitting with a regex `#([A-Za-z0-9_]+)` that matches `#` followed by word characters anywhere in the text. The captured group (index 1) gives the tag name without the `#`.

**Verified against all test cases:**

| Input | Old | New |
|---|---|---|
| `"hello #world #swift"` | `["world", "swift"]` | `["world", "swift"]` ✓ |
| `"just plain text"` | `[]` | `[]` ✓ |
| `"hello,#tag."` | `[]` | `["tag"]` ✓ |
| `"(#foo)"` | `[]` | `["foo"]` ✓ |
| `"multiple #one,#two;#three"` | `[]` | `["one", "two", "three"]` ✓ |
| `"plain #simple text"` | `["simple"]` | `["simple"]` ✓ |
| `"no tags here"` | `[]` | `[]` ✓ |

Tags are returned in the order they appear in the text (regex matches are ordered). No regressions.

